            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Space goblin junkers lurk within the junkyards of Botscrap, the engineering bays of the Sparks, or the winding mazes of Pipetown. With a love of creation matched only by their skill at destruction, some of these goblins form junkbandit gangs to make off with big, shiny pieces of tech. This stolen tech then serves core functions in whatever new technological wonder they're plotting to build next.</p><h2>Space Goblins</h2><p>Goblins are relatively common throughout Absalom Station. Their love of cramped, dark places makes the back alleys and pipelines of the station exceptionally appealing to them. Many goblins are content to live among the populace as merchants, artisans, and cartoonists (with a growing number of goblin publishing houses producing wordless and individualistic \"gobbo-comix\"), but other goblins have a tendency to make trouble. Some of these tricky troublemakers cause blackouts, fires, and even-greater problems throughout Absalom Station.</p>",
            "publication": {
